  "pipeline": {
    "source": "Linux x86-64 Blender 5.2.2 LTS. Source blend archives embed their images. Original high library images also resolve from the model folder.",
    "bake": "Cycles CPU, final triangulated receiver, 2048x2048, isolated matched parts, selected-to-active tangent NORMAL and unlit EMIT. Assembled contact AO uses 12 rays and a 26 mm range. Independent receiver material corrects adjacent-face projections over 12 degrees.",
    "maps": "KTX-Software 4.4.2, glTF-compatible UASTC and Zstandard, all 12 mip levels. Four map payloads and four matching PNG fallbacks embedded.",
    "validation": "Both independently packaged Linux candidates passed the scoped GLB and decoded RGBA8 validator, including the positive-area overlap and planar normal checks. Blender reimport sampled the eight-second sweep and crystal motion. Exact imported pedestal triangles match the closed support and calibrated foot geometry. Decoded level-zero probes establish dielectric graphite and composite fields and metallic ribs. Reimport reports matched across clean builds.",
    "views": "Blender 5.2.2 EEVEE on Apple Silicon, 24 samples, 768x768 fixed paired front/isometric/detail/underside. Low views use actual re-imported GLB and the decoded KTX2 level zero. Motion uses 12 overhead samples at 384x384.",
    "determinism": "Two fresh Linux x86-64 Blender 5.2.2 Cycles CPU bakes and KTX-Software 4.4.2 encodes produced byte-identical PNGs, KTX2 maps, GLB, staged glTF JSON and binary, geometry report and Core-only manifest. Logical high and low scene hashes matched across the two editable pairs. Binary archive hashes below identify the retained first set."
  },
  "corrections": [
    "The F4 review scored the initial Core 78/100 and identified its straight pedestal, bright panel fields and continuous flared foot. The revision uses inward-sloping lower planes, a recessed service belly, four closed contact pads, graphite shoulder faces and carbon cassette inserts. Paired titanium ribs carry the main vertical highlights."
  ],
